## Smart Suggestions vs Research Agents

| | Smart Suggestions (free) | Research Agents (pro) |
|---|---|---|
| How | Rule-based: perturbations, scale sweeps | LLM-driven: reads results, forms hypotheses |
| Requires API key | No | Yes |
| Finds ±10% improvements | Yes | Yes |
| Discovers new approaches | No | Yes |
| Fixes failures | No | Yes (auto-diagnose + patch) |
| Evolves code | No | Yes (modifies train script) |

## Pro Roles

orze-pro ships 6 autonomous roles, each composing from bundled SOPs:

| Role | What it does |
|------|-------------|
| **research** | Reads results, forms hypotheses, designs experiments |
| **professor** | Cross-domain search, idea review, strategy, gap closure |
| **engineer** | Implements ideas, fixes bugs in training code |
| **code_evolution** | Modifies train.py when stuck on a plateau |
| **meta_research** | Adjusts research strategy based on progress |
| **fsm** | Finite state machine that orchestrates all other roles |

```bash
orze sop list                      # see all available SOPs
```

## How It Works

```bash
# Same command — pro features activate automatically:
orze start
# ✓ Research agent reads results and proposes novel ideas
# ✓ Auto-fixes failures and retries
# ✓ Evolves train script when stuck on a plateau
# ✓ The Professor searches literature and reviews strategy
# ✓ You sleep. Experiments run.
```

Zero config change — same `orze.yaml`. Pro features activate on install.

## Compatibility

| orze | orze-pro | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| 4.6.x | 0.13.x | Current release |

## Research campaign boundaries

Orze-pro is a research harness, not a general agent platform. Research roles
default to evidence/file tools without unrestricted shell access, each Claude
invocation defaults to 20 turns, and unsafe permission bypass is opt-in. The
engineer role is the deliberate exception because its job is to test code changes.

Finite campaigns can impose durable attempt budgets. A failed launch or daemon
crash remains charged:

```yaml
research_budget:
  max_agent_attempts: 200

roles:
  research:
    max_attempts: 80
    max_turns: 12
```

Optional hard envelopes are backend-specific: built-in `mode: research` roles
support `max_total_tokens` plus `tokens_per_agent_attempt`; `mode: claude` roles
support `max_cost_usd` plus `cost_usd_per_agent_attempt` through Claude's
`--max-budget-usd`. Unsupported combinations fail closed. Reservations are in
`.orze/state/agent_attempts.jsonl`, completed attempts in `agent_usage.jsonl`, and
provider usage in `llm_usage.jsonl`. OpenAI-compatible streaming records include
cache-read and reasoning-token counts when the provider exposes them, and a
stream is committed only after its `[DONE]` sentinel; truncated streams are
reported as provider failures instead of being parsed as partial research.

Meta-research and bundled SOPs stage validated proposals under
`.orze/policy/proposals/`; they never directly edit active rules. Promotion is
explicit (or requires `meta_research.auto_apply: true`), and a checksum-verified
recorded version can be restored with `meta_research --rollback`.

